Low to moderate. I found no hidden full Russian translation. What I did add to the sweep:
- exact contents and page ranges of Gvozdeva's 2004 excerpts (about 30 pp. over 5 authors);
- the Latyshev 1904 and ВДИ 1949 one-line item;
- passage-level translations in recent articles by Gvozdeva and Kirillova;
- a negative check on the 1953 Struve anthology.
On the English side, Campbell 2000 is confirmed as a full Latin–English edition (still under copyright). New beyond the sweep:
- the near-complete French coverage (CAR series and Budé);
- German coverage of Hyginus Gromaticus (2018);
- Libertini's Liber coloniarum in English and Italian.
The sweep's statuses (RU partial, EN full) stand, with more detail. Priority drops because project criterion (2), 'ideally no English', fails outright.

series:belgorod.notes:
Coverage and limits:
(1) Search engines were unavailable: the WebSearch budget was spent, DuckDuckGo and Mojeek returned captchas, Bing returned junk and Brave returned 429. The list is therefore built from primary documents rather than search results: the PDFs listed on the faculty page https://if.bsuedu.ru/science/publication.php (КВТ 2007–2023, Кондаковские чтения, Иресиона, Эргастирий IV, Византийский клуб Альманах 2018–2023, Lydus monograph 2022), the BelSU DSpace (http://dspace.bsuedu.ru; also Эргастирий I–II), CyberLeninka's article lists for Via in tempore 2008–2026, Crossref, the RSL catalogue, the series PDFs on ancient-life.ru, and ru.wikipedia.
(2) The series «Мир поздней античности» reached 20 issues (2014–2024) according to the 2025 jubilee article (Via in tempore 52(1)). Issues 1–11 were inspected directly. Issues 12–16 are identified only through citations, so their contents and translators are not verified. Issues 17–20 (2021–2024) could not be identified at all.
(3) The scope of Choricius, Риторические сочинения (Эпицентр 2022, 343 pp.) is not verified. Альманах 2023 calls it a complete translation of all his works. Orations I–VIII are independently verified in КВТ 2017–2019.
(4) Many items were made from, or with heavy use of, English versions:
 - Malalas I–VI explicitly from Jeffreys et al. 1986;
 - Himerius with Penella's titles;
 - Aeneas' Theophrastus and Zacharias' Ammonius with notes after Gertz–Dillon–Russell;
 - Fulgentius' Expositio after Whitbread;
 - Ps.-Zachariah probably via Greatrex;
 - Corippus' Iohannis: the basis is not stated.
 Check each item's basis before treating it as a translation from the original.
(5) No Belgorod translation found for: Libanius' letters (only the 2015 anthology of old translations); Libanius' declamations (Радченко 2022 only lists their themes); Lydus De magistratibus III apart from III.25–30, De mensibus I and most of IV, De ostentis beyond the introduction; Procopius of Gaza Ep. 11–174 (the 2020 vol. 15 may contain more); Photius cod. 186–280; Fulgentius Mitologiae I.2, 5–6, 12–15, 17.
(6) КВТ 2022 and 2023 have no translation sections, and Кондаковские чтения VI (2019) has none. Volumes after 2023 were not checked: КВТ 2024–2025, Альманах 2024+, Кондаковские чтения VIII. Pre-2009 volumes are known only through the ru.wikipedia bibliography of the Zosimus translation (Античный мир 1999, Иресиона 2006, Мир Византии 2007).
(7) Via in tempore 2019–2026 (Crossref and CyberLeninka titles) shows no translation publications. CyberLeninka indexes the older Научные ведомости issues only partially, so a few journal translations from 2010–2019 may be missing.
